// concepts.memql -- the __PRODUCT__ product pack (starter).
//
// One concept so the pack contributes a real, queryable schema to the engine's
// concept registry the same way a core domain does. Grow this file with the
// product's own concepts.
//
// Authorization (owned tier): ownerUserId is the per-row authz key -- the same
// pattern every owned core concept uses. A read path filters on
// ownerUserId == actor.userId; a write path stamps it from actor.userId. The
// field models an authz-sane concept, not just an empty schema.
//
// Account: a greeting belongs to the account its author was working in when
// they made it (@belongsTo(account)). The engine fills accountId in at insert
// and keeps it from then on; __PRODUCT_CAMEL__CreateGreeting does not take it.
// It records, and opens the row to nobody. Every concept added to this file
// declares a @belongsTo of its own, saying which account its rows belong to or
// that they belong to none: the engine's docs/public/language/memql.md, "Which
// account a row belongs to", lists the forms. Engine 0.31.35 is the first that
// knows the annotation and an older one refuses it, so a product pinned below
// that moves its ENGINE_REF first.
//
// The concept id assembles from @version + the domain namespace + the
// name into v1:__PRODUCT_ID__:greeting. The namespace uses __PRODUCT_ID__ (the
// identifier-safe product form, hyphens -> underscores): the engine's namespace
// pattern is [a-z][a-z0-9_]* so a hyphenated product would otherwise fail to
// register (#38). The DSL directory also uses __PRODUCT_ID__, so the
// directory and namespace agree without a namespace.pin override. Two products
// can therefore bind their own greeting shapes even on the released engine.
// Ids on the wire are bare short slugs (the engine bare-ifies at
// its seams; clients never compose canonical ids), so this schema declares no
// canonical-id @pattern anywhere -- per the A1 inbound-hardening rule the engine
// conformance now enforces.

@version("1.0.0")
@description("A starter greeting record contributed by the __PRODUCT__ pack. Demonstrates that a pack's embedded .memql concept lands in the engine's concept registry alongside the core domains. Replace with the product's own concepts.")
@displayCard(primary="message", secondary="ownerUserId", tertiary="createdAt")
@belongsTo(account)
concept greeting {
  ownerUserId  string  @required  @description("v1:identity:user.id of the owner. Per-row authz key (owned tier); stamped from actor.userId by the writing mutation.")
  message      string  @required  @description("The greeting text, e.g. \"hello from the __PRODUCT__ pack\".")
  accountId    string  @description("The account this row belongs to (see @belongsTo). The engine fills it in at insert and carries it forward on every update.")
}
